{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/238977-immortal-the-gathering-20th-anniversary-edition","id":238977,"title":"Immortal: The Gathering 20th Anniversary Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-24T02:07:13-07:00","id":238977,"title":"Immortal: The Gathering 20th Anniversary Edition","content":"Hi guys, I'm working on updating the Immorrtal: The Gathering (also called Highlander: The Gathering) fan splat to x20 standards, giving it the old spit and polish. I've set up a blog for the development but I'm going to mirror all my posts in this thread along with answering any questions with it. I released it here on the forums a while back, but I changed a bunch of things since then, and I want to make a dedicated thread for it where I constantly update the system and actually talk.<br /> <br /> Here's the blog for your reading - <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/</a><br /> Here's the download page that I will always update with the newest edition - <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/2014/08/download-page.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://immortalthegathering.blogspot...load-page.html</a><br /> Here's the latest post - <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/2014/08/immortal-gathering-20th-anniversary.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://immortalthegathering.blogspot...niversary.html</a><br /> <br /> I really value feedback, and feel free to tear me a new one, I'm not gonna go complain to Ian or the Mod team because someone on the internet doesn't like my work. I do ask that if you are going to state a problem that you at least attempt to give a remedy to it, if you can't no big deal, but yelling doesn't solve problems. I'm also hugely open to suggestions, questions, and the likes, so feel free to ask me anything from how my day is to the Semi-Empirical Mass Formula, I'll attempt to answer them to the best of my knowledge! Please at least open the splat and read it to completion before you complain about it though, I've changed quite a bit since the first edition came out in 1993, so it might not be the one you remember. Any feedback is better than no feedback to me. Also remember, this splat is based on a product of its time and I tried to preserve that, so take it with a grain of salt, and it reads better if you rewatch the first move then read it but you don't have to!<br /> <br /> Also big shout out to Mr. Gone for his help! You're a wonderful man and I hope you die old and with many children, surrounded by people who love and care for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Greetings people, I'm the developer of the 20th Anniversary Edition of the Classic World of Darkness fan splat Immortal: The Gathering, previously called Highlander: The Gathering. I take the handle of Outlander and I'm found on a variety of sites including the Onyx Path forums, Roll20, and /tg/. Now that introductions are over, let me talk about what I'm on about.<br /> <br /> <b>Why are you updating this?</b><br /> <br /> Well this is a popular splat that's was made way back in the 90's with the help of a White Wolf Freelancer, and it's one of, if not the, best known Classic World of Darkness fan splats. It's most noted problem was balanced and other such interactions with other lines, but it's still a great and fun splat to play. I love the splat personally and think it's always fun to shove it in another game line because it's so damn awesome.<br /> <br /> <b>What did you change?</b><br /> <br /> Well I didn't change too much, the biggest change over the Revised edition of Immortal: The Gathering is the addition of Dark Quickening as a morality system. Dark Quickening was in the Revised system to a degree, but didn't encapsulate a morality system. This system is basically a copy paste of Demon: The Fallen's system of morality, which is far looser and is a constant struggle to keep balance. I also added more than just morality, I followed the 20th Anniversary's idea for the metaplot which is agnostic approach, going with the belief that the splat should work with <i>ANY</i> other CWoD splat. Just being able to put an Immortal inside any of splat and having it work well seems like it can make any game more fun to me, especially when the Immortal goes through the process of First Death during the game and has to come to terms with immortality with other Supernaturals who are equally as confused. The more character development that can be added to a game, the more interesting the game it is to me, which is one of my goals.<br /> I removed some other things to the game, however. One of the major things I said above was making it metaplot agnostic, as such I removed all connection to the movies beyond quotes and other such things to the movies and series. I want Immortals to seem rare and unique, less than 500 in a world of 7 billion people, and by having established characters, I think this hurts this idea. As such I have left this all up to the Storyteller to make and decide. Immortal duels should be rare, at random or an entire story building up to a fight, and make the game more interesting; they should not be a Dungeons and Dragons style murderfest to level up and get stronger.<br /> One of the other most important things I did was balance and rule clarifications, or I at least tried. I picked the most important things from movies and series, and gave them a healthy touch from the World of Darkness. Immortals aren't as unstoppable as they used to be in previous editions. I changed the healing chart speeds to make them not healing tanks. Their powers are now come with a cost, they get tired and get weakened after pushing their bodies to the limit for fighting and super strength. No longer are they completely unstoppable, least not till Elder tier.<br /> <br /> <b>What's next?</b><br /> <br /> I have spent the past ~4 months working on the system and the character sheet, which I feel is a usable update to the system. I reworked the duel system to work not only with the new versions, but with other Supernaturals. Here's the list of stuff I feel I need to work on. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Balance powers more. I can't clarify this enough, and I'm working a lot on this to balance the system. I love feedback, so feel free to bitch.</li> <li>Editing. I've been pretty lax in this regard, but I feel like this is an important thing.</li> <li>Work more on power interactions between splats. I have a huge ass page of these and it's still not enough.</li> <li>Add more to the Storyteller chapter. I don't have nearly enough for this I believe. I'd love to add more ties between the splats like Demons seeing them a Malhim of some type, how Vampires interact with them, and their relationship with the Traditions and Technocracy. I'd also like to add more ideas for PC's and major NPC's that involve them; Technocrat super soldier who died on the table and triggered his First Death, Vampire ghoul who died during his embrace and woke up neither Human or Vampire. More fun things like this. Including more stuff about how to run an all Immortal game and how to make each of them feel <i>unique </i>which is very important to me.</li> <li>More on favored weapons. An Immortal's blade is like a third arm to him, and is fundamentally part of his soul. It's super important to their character. I'd like to expand upon this and make this a more important part of the character beyond being just a weapon.</li> <li>More Immortal unique abilities and backgrounds. Immortals are extremely strange, their bodies are like a normal human, but their powers are beyond that. I want to make an Immortal able to do more super human things beyond just a swinging a sword faster and moving quickly. Highlander The Search of Vengeance is a huge inspiration to this for me. I'll probably go diving through the Hunter books and some older splats for lost abilities and backgrounds that help with this, along with other new merits.</li> <li>Add more Merits and Flaws. I feel like I have a lot here but there's never enough neat ideas that can be done with such a unique character in my belief.</li> <li>More inclusion for Hedge Magic. One of the largest things I noticed with Immortals is the lack of magic to them. They might be nearly indestructible but they can't even see a Vampire with Obfuscate. They have little to no magical defenses beyond their passive powers. Hedge Magic combined with the Quickening can make for even more unique characters in my opinion, like an Immortal Sorcerer who runs a society of Sorcerers that tries to help humanity or destroy them. Magic is superbly used in the Highlander fluff and I feel like that's important to remember.</li> </ol><br /> <b>Where's the current edition?</b><br /> <br /> I will always have a page devoted to the most current version of the splat. I will update it with some change log notes on a new blog post when I do. I'll post the newest version, 0.21, soon. And I love feedback, so feel free to vent your rage or passion in the comments, /tg/, or OPP forums.<br /> <br /> -Outlander<br /> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T06:16:14-07:00","id":239058,"title":"","content":"I think you should remove the World Trade Center from the Pain Tolerance Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3117-lucius","name":"Lucius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T10:36:03-07:00","id":239317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/238977-immortal-the-gathering-20th-anniversary-edition?p=239058#post239058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you should remove the World Trade Center from the Pain Tolerance Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>As bad as that does seem, it still does fit the merit's description and the text does predate the whole event. Though I should probably update it to keep in line with timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T13:37:56-07:00","id":266970,"title":"","content":"Got some work done and updated the page: <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/2014/09/updated-page.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://immortalthegathering.blogspot...ated-page.html</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the book has been updated a bit, fixed a few things and added some stuff. Here's the majority of the patch notes.<br /> <br /> Change log:<ul><li>Added a Storyteller chapter that is very basic and covers a bit on VtM, WtA, and MtA<ul><li>Goes a bit into why to play and how to do cross overs with some ideas</li> </ul></li> <li>Changed the rules for healing so they're in line with normal WoD rules for healing, bottom to top and all. ~2 hours to heal all the way, technically 1:53:03 but it's about the same that I felt it's fine.</li> <li>Changed rules for Heal Self obviously</li> <li>Clarified the rules for Empower Self and fixed a major typo</li> <li>Added more rules for Favored Weapons and multiple weapons</li> <li>Added rules for enchanting an Immortal's favored weapon</li> <li>Added rules for Imbued and their Edges</li> <li>Changed starting Virtues from 3 to 5</li> <li>Altered character sheet to account for change in this Virtue change</li> </ul><br /> Going to keep working and will update the game until I think it's good enough.<br /> <br /> Reason to drink: DAV20 and M20 are almost out. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T22:43:59-08:00","id":313513,"title":"","content":"Got some more work done in my free time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>What's new</b><br /><br /> So the book has been updated a bit, fixed a few things and added some stuff. Here's the majority of the patch notes.<br /> <br /> Change log:<ul><li>Added to the Storyteller chapter a bit</li> <li>Tried to fix more typos and clarified rules</li> <li>Added a new Quickening 6 power: Summoning the Loyal Steel</li> </ul><br /> Going to keep working and will update the game until I think it's good enough.<br /> <br /> Reason to drink: Exalted 3e is slowly working towards done </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:23:59-07:00","id":742328,"title":"","content":"Wow I haven't updated this in a long time. Well I finally got my rules updated though with the release of M20. You want your sword to be a Wonder? Well the rules now support that better, just try to avoid the Quiet.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/2015/10/update-027.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://immortalthegathering.blogspot...pdate-027.html</a> <b>Update time!</b><br /><br /> So it's been a while since I did an update on here. This is probably one of the larger updates I've done. I tuned up some of the rules, updated them for Mage 20th, and backtracked on power nerfings. The biggest thing I did was reducing the levels needed for certain powers.<ul><li>Empower Blade is now a level 1 power</li> <li>Empower self is now a level 2</li> <li>Speed of the Stag is now level 3</li> <li>And Power Strike is now the level 4 power.</li> <li>Empower Self also lets you exceed trait max for certain periods of time at the cost of more exhaustion.</li> </ul><br /> I also updated the character sheet to make it less torturous to use. All in all there's a lot of stuff I did in this update. The download always works too, so enjoy the fun. </div> </div> </div>Not sure how the new Highlander reboot will affect the rules though if it's actually not terrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T04:01:32-08:00","id":768405,"title":"","content":"Hay Outlander, I am so glad someone other than me remembers Highlander, and played it in the D10 system. I have been playing a Demon the Fallen game for two months now, and after seeing how torment works, I thought it would be a nice fit in an Immortal game. So, kudos on the adaptation to V20 rules, and a big hearty thank you.<br /> <br /> Also will be running a game (using your book) this weekend. The game will be a monthly meeting, as such my commets will be quite spaced out. One question, have you had anyone play test the duel combat rules yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9469-jacklando","name":"JackLando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9469_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T20:12:06-08:00","id":773603,"title":"","content":"Do you plan on adding any notable NPCs to this endeavor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T10:08:20-08:00","id":781183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackLando</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/238977-immortal-the-gathering-20th-anniversary-edition?p=768405#post768405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hay Outlander, I am so glad someone other than me remembers Highlander, and played it in the D10 system. I have been playing a Demon the Fallen game for two months now, and after seeing how torment works, I thought it would be a nice fit in an Immortal game. So, kudos on the adaptation to V20 rules, and a big hearty thank you.<br /> <br /> Also will be running a game (using your book) this weekend. The game will be a monthly meeting, as such my commets will be quite spaced out. One question, have you had anyone play test the duel combat rules yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>So I've been away from the forums for a long while, and some reason this went to my junk box, so sorry for the 2 week plus response time.<br /> Anyways, yes I've done a lot of testing with the dueling system. It works well for what it is. However I've only updated bits and pieces of it, the original version dates back to the 90's, which was stolen off the Klaive combat system from Werewolf. More of the story, the system works fine so long as the duel is done on even terms. Twice now, an Immortal died because they botched their initiative roll while the other guy did amazingly. Nothing really can be done about that since that's just dumb luck getting involved. It's not until Quickening 5+ that things get really wacky. And at that point they should be wacky. Just watch your ass when fighting high Dark Quickening Immortals since they get a lot of extra dice for Quickening rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you plan on adding any notable NPCs to this endeavor? </div> </div> </div>Originally the characters from the movies were statted out, but I felt like the stats were far too out of date for the system. My goal with the system is to provide a framework to play the game in, and not shove the plot of the movies into it, so I purposely didn't update them. Were I to update them, they'd probably be Quickening 8-9 monsters of death and destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T12:07:11-08:00","id":781781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/238977-immortal-the-gathering-20th-anniversary-edition?p=781183#post781183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I've been away from the forums for a long while, and some reason this went to my junk box, so sorry for the 2 week plus response time.<br /> Anyways, yes I've done a lot of testing with the dueling system. It works well for what it is. However I've only updated bits and pieces of it, the original version dates back to the 90's, which was stolen off the Klaive combat system from Werewolf. More of the story, the system works fine so long as the duel is done on even terms. Twice now, an Immortal died because they botched their initiative roll while the other guy did amazingly. Nothing really can be done about that since that's just dumb luck getting involved. It's not until Quickening 5+ that things get really wacky. And at that point they should be wacky. Just watch your ass when fighting high Dark Quickening Immortals since they get a lot of extra dice for Quickening rolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> Originally the characters from the movies were statted out, but I felt like the stats were far too out of date for the system. My goal with the system is to provide a framework to play the game in, and not shove the plot of the movies into it, so I purposely didn't update them. Were I to update them, they'd probably be Quickening 8-9 monsters of death and destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little disappointed, because I had done some immortals from the series: The Four Horsemen (Kronos, Methos, Silas, and Caspian), Grayson, Kalas, Cassandra, Amanda, Fitzcairn, and Darius; and I had hoped to offer them....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:25:07-08:00","id":819358,"title":"","content":"Question, will the Immortal RPG be updated with example characters and will be updated when the edition of Vampire comes out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11118-gmellos","name":"gmellos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}